# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps the *host's* build output out of it.
# Copying a Windows-built obj/ into a Linux image poisons the restore: project.assets.json records
# absolute host paths and the wrong RID, and `dotnet publish` then fails or silently reuses stale
# assemblies. Everything below is either regenerated inside the image or irrelevant to it.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/TestResults/

.git/
.github/
.claude/

# Local-only credentials. They must never reach an image layer — they are supplied at run time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests are not published; the CI workflow runs them.
tests/

docs/
*.md
!README.md

docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
Chat.slnLaunch*
*.pdf
